{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And behold, horns [karan].</b> For his light shone from the radiance of the Shekhinah — and likewise: ״קרנים מידו לו״. And it seems to me that when the light shone, it resembled a ram whose horns are split, branching this way and that, and this is the meaning of the term קרן. And because they erred and wanted to appoint a leader in his place, the Holy One, blessed be He, illuminated him with the radiance of His Shekhinah, to show them that there was no leader as worthy as him."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The Hebrew text contains apparent typos (הבקר for הבהיק, מתפצל for מתפצלות); translated as intended. קרנים מידו לו quotes Habakkuk 3:4."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:44.059332493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}